First,You must understand your "flavor",For Example:

=====Cert Licence Begin=====
Name:My first cert
Date:20250501
Issuer:CodeBlue-Develop
Description:My first cert
PID:0123456789.......23232ABDc303203DJIFi#rie(Many Word)
=====Cert Licence End=====

But is it too easy for a hacker to crack it (if the certificate expires, just change the date)
so,PPPPPPPPPPPPPP      IIIIIIIIII       DDDDDDDDD
   P            P           I           D        D
   P            P           I           D         D
   PPPPPPPPPPPPPP           I           D         D
   P                        I           D        D
   P                   IIIIIIIIII       DDDDDDDDD
comes in handy!
Therefore, it is necessary to identify whether the certificate name, certificate issuance date, and certificate issuer/organization correspond to the PID.
Of course, that's not enough. If so, does that mean that as long as the name is the same and the date is the same, can the same promulgator apply the same PID?
That's why we need one, the identification code!
The identification code can be customised to your own "taste".
For Example:
ckcks-q3fs3-sddfs-serde-332ds
Then,the cert becomes:

=====Cert Licence Begin=====
Name:My first cert
Date:20250501
Issuer:CodeBlue-Develop
Description:My first cert
PID:0123456789.......23232ABDc303203DJIFi#rie
Sign:ckcks-q3fs3-sddfs-serde-332ds
=====Cert Licence End=====
All right!
Then, you can do the Pid and Sign verification procedures well based on your own ”taste“.

Epilogue:用英文写教程文件，真是太！难！了！
